{
  "id": "aulaf75",
  "name": "Aula F75 (258a:010c)",
  "note": "75%: 6 key rows. `row` here is the VISUAL row (0 = F-row) so 2D effects place keys correctly, but the board's LED index counts the F-row LAST, not first: hardware index 0 is the number row (same as hive65) and the F-row sits in each column's leftover 6th slot. Hence slot = col*6 + row for rows 1..5, and col*6 + 6 for the F-row. Confirmed on hardware: driving slots 6/12/18/36/60/66 lights esc/f1/f2/f5/f9/f10. Main-block slots are byte-identical to hive65. Still unverified: the knob (col 15 -> 96), and whether f11/f12 are really in cols 11/12 -- f12 sits physically over backspace, so col 13 (slot 84) is the alternative. Map with `keyboardrgb.py walk --profile aulaf75`.",
